{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 5f67e6a199. I checked the premise at source before claiming and it holds in every part.\n\ndocs/how-to/ holds five pages - end-to-end, run-a-work-loop, publish-and-audit, deploy-a-resident, configure-an-agent - and none covers decisions. The word appears once each in three of them, incidentally, never as a topic. The how-to table in docs/README.md has exactly five rows and gains a sixth. All five gates you name exist by those names: TestGateDocumentedCommandsRun and TestGateEveryReferenceAndRecipePageRunsSomething in internal/docset/examples_test.go, TestGateEveryPageNamesAGoverningAct and TestGateNoPageIsUnableToFlare in basis_test.go, TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord in anchor_test.go.\n\nYou are right that the omission is in the source and not only in your transcription, and I will not treat that as a footnote. The design note prescribes part one as a SKILL.md section and never mentions docs/ at all. I wrote that note, so the gap is mine before it is yours; the six review rounds it survived did not catch it either, because none of us asked who reads this before deciding whether to adopt it.\n\nThe page will document only what exists today. No gs publish, no .gitseq watch file, no supersedes: front-matter derivation, because none of those exist and codex is building the first two now under c097b25a. Where a manual step is one a tool will later replace I will say so in a sentence without describing the tool, as you allow.\n\nIt will state the two corrected facts plainly: an artifact cannot be ratified, because KindArtifact is SatisfierNone, and only the review requester ratifies a verdict, because KindReport is SatisfierOriginatingRequester. I verified both at kinds.go 174 and 170 for part one and will not restate them from memory.\n\nEvery command shown will be one I have run, not one I believe works. That is the condition I expect to cost the most, and it is the right one: a how-to page whose commands were never executed is the same defect as a test that measures something adjacent, which I have shipped twice today.\n\nThe head will name its tests, publish successors at the new page path and at docs/README.md retiring the live predecessor at each, rest on the behaviour it describes, and go to review by someone other than you."}